<section id="about" style="background:var(--white)">
<div data-stack="2" style="max-width:1280px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(56px,8vw,96px) clamp(18px,4vw,32px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:70px;align-items:start">
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:22px;max-width:720px">
<span style="color:var(--gold);font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase">College Station, TX Audiologists &amp; Hearing Aids</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-size:clamp(36px,3.6vw,54px);font-weight:800;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.045em">Liberty Hearing Center</h2>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; text-wrap: pretty">We're a locally owned audiology practice serving College Station and the greater Brazos Valley. From pediatric hearing screenings to VA C&amp;P evaluations and custom hearing solutions, we're committed to helping you stay connected to the people and moments that matter most.</p>
<p style="margin:0;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Our audiologists, Dr. Chris Duhon, AuD, and Dr. Carly Hall, AuD, bring a warm, unhurried approach to every appointment. We want to know who you are, where you're from, and what your hearing challenges look like in your daily life — because the right solution starts with the right conversation.</p>
<p style="margin:0;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">We serve families, children, adults, veterans, musicians, and working professionals throughout College Station and the Brazos Valley. As a locally owned practice, we are invested in this community for the long haul, and we treat every patient — regardless of background or budget — with the same level of care and respect.</p>
</div>
<div style="align-self:end;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px">
<a href="/dr-chris-duhon/" data-stack="2" style="overflow:hidden;display:grid;grid-template-columns:170px 1fr;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--white);transition:.3s" style-hover="transform:translateY(-6px);box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<img src="/assets/dr-chris.webp" alt="Dr. Chris Duhon, AuD" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 18%" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:9px;padding:26px">
<h3 style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-size:22px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.02em">Dr. Chris Duhon, AuD</h3>
<span style="color:var(--gold);font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase">Doctor of Audiology</span>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;text-wrap:pretty">A warm, unhurried approach to every appointment — from pediatric screenings to VA C&amp;P evaluations and custom hearing solutions.</p>
</div>
</a>
<a href="/dr-carly-hall/" data-stack="2" style="overflow:hidden;display:grid;grid-template-columns:170px 1fr;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--white);transition:.3s" style-hover="transform:translateY(-6px);box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<img src="/assets/dr-carly.webp" alt="Dr. Carly Hall, AuD" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 18%" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:9px;padding:26px">
<h3 style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-size:22px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.02em">Dr. Carly Hall, AuD</h3>
<span style="color:var(--gold);font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase">Doctor of Audiology</span>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;text-wrap:pretty">Starts with the conversation — who you are, where you're from, and what hearing challenges look like in your daily life.</p>
</div>
</a>
</div>
</div>
<div style="max-width:1280px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 32px 96px">
<div data-stack="2" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:.85fr 1.15fr;gap:70px;align-items:start;padding:40px 44px;border-radius:24px;background:var(--white);box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11);border-top:4px solid var(--gold)">
<div>
<span style="display:block;margin-bottom:10px;color:var(--gold);font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase">Service &amp; community discounts</span>
<p style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-size:23px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.03em;text-wrap:pretty">A thank-you to those who serve.</p>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px">
<p style="margin:0;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">As a token of appreciation for those who serve, we're proud to offer special discounts on hearing technology to active-duty military, veterans, law enforcement officers, firefighters, nurses, EMTs, and all Brazos Valley ISD employees — including teachers, classroom support staff, paraprofessionals, bus drivers, cafeteria staff, custodial staff, and campus-based employees.</p>
<p style="margin:0;padding:18px 22px;border-radius:14px;background:rgba(var(--gold-rgb),.09);color:var(--navy);font-size:16px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.7;text-wrap:pretty"><span style="color:var(--gold)">Special Offer:</span> Up to $500 rebate with 0% 12-month financing for patients in the community appreciation program. Call for more details.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<!-- ================= URGENT CARE SECTION ================= -->
<section class="lhc-urgent">
  <div class="lhc-urgent__inner">
    <div>
      <span class="lhc-urgent__eyebrow">Get Urgent care</span>
      <p class="lhc-urgent__title">Sudden Hearing Loss? <br>Don't Wait.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lhc-urgent__body">
      <p class="lhc-urgent__text">Waking up with unexplained hearing loss in one or both ears can be a medical emergency — not just an inconvenience. The sooner it's diagnosed and treated (ideally within 72 hours to two weeks), the better your chances of recovery. Call us today — we prioritize same-day or next-day appointments for sudden hearing loss.</p>
      <button type="button" class="lhc-urgent__link" data-lhc-modal-open>Learn more <span>→</span></button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= MODAL ================= -->
<div class="lhc-modal" id="lhc-ssnhl-modal" hidden>
  <div class="lhc-modal__backdrop" data-lhc-modal-close></div>
  <div class="lhc-modal__dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="lhc-ssnhl-title">
    <button type="button" class="lhc-modal__close" aria-label="Close" data-lhc-modal-close>✕</button>
    <span class="lhc-modal__eyebrow">Urgent care</span>
    <h2 class="lhc-modal__title" id="lhc-ssnhl-title">Sudden Hearing Loss? Here's What You Need to Know</h2>
    <div class="lhc-modal__body">
      <p>If you woke up and suddenly noticed hearing loss in one or both ears and you know it's not from a concert, gunfire, or other loud noise exposure, it's worth taking seriously. Sudden hearing loss can come from a few different places: a simple mechanical blockage like earwax or fluid behind the eardrum, or something happening deeper in the inner ear itself.</p>
      <p>A second category, sudden sensorineural hearing loss (SSNHL), is the one that requires urgency. It can be triggered by a viral or autoimmune inflammatory response, or by a vascular event that interrupts blood flow to the inner ear, similar in concept to a stroke. Because the inner ear can't be examined just by looking in the ear canal, only a hearing test can tell you which type you're dealing with.</p>
      <p>Timing matters enormously here. The sooner SSNHL is identified and treated (ideally within the first 72 hours to two weeks), the better the odds of recovering meaningful hearing, often with a short course of oral or injected steroids. The longer treatment is delayed, the more those odds decline, and after about a month, the chances of full recovery drop significantly. Unfortunately, this is exactly what we see too often: people wait days or weeks assuming it will resolve on its own, or get bounced between providers before the story is fully heard and the case gets flagged as a true sudden hearing loss.</p>
      <p><strong>What to do:</strong> If you wake up with sudden, unexplained hearing loss in one or both ears, don't wait it out. Call us right away. We prioritize getting patients with sudden hearing loss in for testing as quickly as possible, because in this case, time is hearing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lhc-modal__actions">
      <a class="lhc-btn lhc-btn--primary" href="/book-appointment/">Book Your Appointment</a>
      <a class="lhc-btn lhc-btn--ghost" href="tel:9794507996">Give Us a Call</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<section id="services" style="background:var(--cream)" data-comment-anchor="9312da944d-section">
<div style="max-width:1280px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(56px,8vw,96px) clamp(18px,4vw,32px)">
<div data-stack="2" style="margin-bottom:56px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:.95fr 1.05fr;gap:60px;align-items:center">
<figure id="svc-figure" style="margin:0;overflow:hidden;border-radius:24px;box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)"><img src="/assets/hearing-test.webp" alt="A patient wearing audiometric headphones during a hearing test at Liberty Hearing Center" style="display:block;width:100%;height:clamp(237px,50vw,430px);object-fit:cover;object-position:62% 45%" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
<div>
<h2 style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-size:clamp(36px,3.8vw,56px);font-weight:800;line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.045em">Audiology Services <span style="display:block;margin-top:12px;font-size:.3em;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold)">in College Station, TX</span></h2>
<p style="margin:22px 0 0;max-width:620px;font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;text-wrap:pretty">Our diagnostic services go beyond a standard hearing test. Using advanced technology — real-ear measurements, tympanometry, acoustic reflex testing, and more — we deliver the detailed information needed for accurate diagnosis and personalized treatment at every age.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="svc-accordion" data-stack="2" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:18px;align-items:start">
<details style="padding:30px 34px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-top:4px solid var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));border-radius:14px;background:var(--svc-bg,var(--white));color:var(--svc-text,var(--navy));transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--svc-title,var(--navy));font-size:25px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.03em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));font-size:22px;line-height:1.25">+</span>Hearing Evaluations</summary>
<p style="margin:16px 0 14px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">A comprehensive hearing evaluation is the first step toward better hearing. We test how well you hear across a range of frequencies and identify the type and degree of any hearing loss (including sensorineural, conductive, and mixed hearing loss). We'll walk you through exactly what the results mean for your daily life. We provide evaluations for patients of all ages, from newborns to adults.</p>
<a href="/hearing-evaluations/" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;color:var(--brand-red);font-size:14px;font-weight:750;transition:.3s" style-hover="color:var(--navy)">Learn more <span>→</span></a>
</details>
<details style="padding:30px 34px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-top:4px solid var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));border-radius:14px;background:var(--svc-bg,var(--white));color:var(--svc-text,var(--navy));transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--svc-title,var(--navy));font-size:25px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.03em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));font-size:22px;line-height:1.25">+</span>Pediatric Hearing Evaluation</summary>
<p style="margin:16px 0 14px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Children don't always have the words to tell you when something doesn't sound right. We provide comprehensive pediatric hearing evaluations, including newborn follow-up OAE screenings, ear-specific testing, tympanometry, and advanced ABR/ASSR diagnostic assessments when needed. Visual Reinforcement Audiometry (VRA) is available for infants as young as 4–6 months and Conditioned Play Audiometry for young children. We create a calm, child-friendly environment, using age-appropriate techniques and advanced technology to obtain reliable results for families and referring physicians.</p>
<a href="/pediatric-hearing-testing/" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;color:var(--brand-red);font-size:14px;font-weight:750;transition:.3s" style-hover="color:var(--navy)">Learn more <span>→</span></a>
</details>
<details style="padding:30px 34px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-top:4px solid var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));border-radius:14px;background:var(--svc-bg,var(--white));color:var(--svc-text,var(--navy));transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--svc-title,var(--navy));font-size:25px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.03em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));font-size:22px;line-height:1.25">+</span>Veterans C&amp;P Hearing Evaluations</summary>
<p style="margin:16px 0 14px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">We conduct comprehensive Compensation and Pension (C&amp;P) hearing and tinnitus examinations for veterans authorized through the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs. Every evaluation is thorough, professionally documented, and completed with the respect every veteran deserves.</p>
<a href="/veterans-cp-hearing-evaluations/" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;color:var(--brand-red);font-size:14px;font-weight:750;transition:.3s" style-hover="color:var(--navy)">Learn more <span>→</span></a>
</details>
<details style="padding:30px 34px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-top:4px solid var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));border-radius:14px;background:var(--svc-bg,var(--white));color:var(--svc-text,var(--navy));transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--svc-title,var(--navy));font-size:25px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.03em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));font-size:22px;line-height:1.25">+</span>Musicians' Hearing Evaluations</summary>
<p style="margin:16px 0 14px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Musicians rely on their hearing more than almost any other professional, yet they're also among the most vulnerable to noise-induced hearing loss and tinnitus. Standard hearing tests only measure up to 8kHz, missing early damage that often begins at higher frequencies.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">At Liberty Hearing Center, we offer extended high-frequency testing up to 16kHz, allowing us to detect subtle changes in hearing before they affect your ability to perform, mix, or enjoy music. Regular monitoring helps musicians catch early warning signs, make informed decisions about hearing protection, and preserve the fine pitch and tonal discrimination their careers depend on. We also offer custom-fit musician earplugs and consultations tailored to your instrument, practice habits, and performance environment.</p>
<a href="/custom-hearing-protection-conservation/" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;color:var(--brand-red);font-size:14px;font-weight:750;transition:.3s" style-hover="color:var(--navy)">Learn more <span>→</span></a>
</details>
<details style="padding:30px 34px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-top:4px solid var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));border-radius:14px;background:var(--svc-bg,var(--white));color:var(--svc-text,var(--navy));transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--svc-title,var(--navy));font-size:25px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.03em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));font-size:22px;line-height:1.25">+</span>Customized Ear Protection Solutions</summary>
<p style="margin:16px 0 14px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Not all hearing protection is created equal, and off-the-shelf options often mean sacrificing comfort, safety, or sound quality. At Liberty Hearing Center, we design custom-fit hearing protection tailored to your lifestyle.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">For musicians, we offer custom earplugs with interchangeable 9dB, 15dB, 20dB, and 25dB filters, reducing volume evenly across frequencies so the music stays clear while your hearing stays protected.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">We also fit custom in-ear monitors for singers and performers, giving them full control over the mix — how loud they hear their own vocals, other instruments, and the crowd — for a safer, more precise on-stage experience.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Swimmers and those with ear tubes can benefit from custom swim plugs that help prevent water intrusion and swimmer's ear. For hunters and shooters, we offer custom firearm earplugs that enhance speech and ambient sound during quiet moments, then instantly engage to protect against the sudden, damaging noise of a gunshot.</p>
<a href="/custom-hearing-protection-conservation/" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;color:var(--brand-red);font-size:14px;font-weight:750;transition:.3s" style-hover="color:var(--navy)">Learn more <span>→</span></a>
</details>
<details style="padding:30px 34px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-top:4px solid var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));border-radius:14px;background:var(--svc-bg,var(--white));color:var(--svc-text,var(--navy));transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--svc-title,var(--navy));font-size:25px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.03em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--svc-accent,var(--gold));font-size:22px;line-height:1.25">+</span>Diagnostic Services</summary>
<p style="margin:16px 0 14px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">We provide comprehensive evaluations for patients of all ages, including high-frequency hearing assessments for musicians, ototoxicity monitoring, advanced tympanometry and acoustic reflex testing, newborn hearing evaluations with OAE, ABR, and ASSR technology, pediatric testing (including Visual Reinforcement Audiometry), sudden hearing loss evaluations, hearing aid performance analysis and verification, real-ear measurements, cochlear implant services, and custom hearing protection for musicians, hunters, and others exposed to hazardous noise. Our advanced technology delivers the detailed information needed for accurate diagnosis, personalized treatment, and exceptional hearing healthcare.</p>
