<span style="color:var(--gold);font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase">Good to know</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-size:clamp(34px,3.2vw,48px);font-weight:800;line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-.045em;text-wrap:balance">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px">
<details open="true" style="padding:26px clamp(18px,4vw,32px);border:1px solid var(--cream-border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--white);transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--navy);font-size:21px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.02em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--gold);font-size:20px;line-height:1.3">+</span>I woke up with sudden hearing loss — should I be worried?</summary>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Yes, if there's no obvious cause like loud noise exposure. Sudden hearing loss can signal an inner ear issue that responds well to treatment — but only if caught early, ideally within the first 72 hours to two weeks. Call us right away so we can test your hearing and get you connected to treatment fast.</p>
</details>
<details style="padding:26px clamp(18px,4vw,32px);border:1px solid var(--cream-border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--white);transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--navy);font-size:21px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.02em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--gold);font-size:20px;line-height:1.3">+</span>What audiology services do you provide?</summary>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">We provide comprehensive hearing care for patients of all ages, including adult and pediatric hearing evaluations, newborn hearing screenings, veteran C&amp;P examinations, tinnitus evaluations, hearing aid fittings, cochlear implant programming, ear wax removal, and custom hearing protection.</p>
</details>
<details style="padding:26px clamp(18px,4vw,32px);border:1px solid var(--cream-border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--white);transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--navy);font-size:21px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.02em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--gold);font-size:20px;line-height:1.3">+</span>Do you serve veterans?</summary>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Yes. We conduct VA-authorized Compensation and Pension (C&amp;P) examinations, evaluating hearing loss and tinnitus for veterans in the College Station and Brazos Valley area. We also extend special discount pricing on hearing technology to active-duty military and veterans as part of our service appreciation program.</p>
</details>
<details style="padding:26px clamp(18px,4vw,32px);border:1px solid var(--cream-border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--white);transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--navy);font-size:21px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.02em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--gold);font-size:20px;line-height:1.3">+</span>What hearing aid brands do you carry?</summary>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">We carry hearing aids from Phonak, Oticon, ReSound, Widex, Starkey, and Signia, and we match each patient with devices that fit their specific hearing loss, lifestyle, and budget, and every fitting includes real-ear verification to confirm the devices are calibrated correctly for each of your ears.</p>
</details>
<details style="padding:26px clamp(18px,4vw,32px);border:1px solid var(--cream-border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--white);transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--navy);font-size:21px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.02em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--gold);font-size:20px;line-height:1.3">+</span>What pediatric hearing services do you offer?</summary>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">We provide a full range of pediatric hearing services, including OAE-based newborn follow-up screenings, Visual Reinforcement Audiometry (VRA) for infants as young as 4–6 months, ABR and ASSR testing for children who need objective measures, and diagnostic evaluations for school-age children who do not pass school hearing screenings or have concerns about speech and language development.</p>
</details>
<details style="padding:26px clamp(18px,4vw,32px);border:1px solid var(--cream-border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--white);transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--navy);font-size:21px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.02em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--gold);font-size:20px;line-height:1.3">+</span>Do you accept insurance?</summary>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">We accept Medicare, Blue Cross Blue Shield, United Healthcare, and authorized referrals through the VA Community Care Network. We'll verify your benefits and explain any out-of-pocket costs before your appointment so there are no surprises. Contact us to learn more.</p>
</details>
<details style="padding:26px clamp(18px,4vw,32px);border:1px solid var(--cream-border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--white);transition:.3s" style-hover="box-shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(var(--navy-rgb),.11)">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:var(--navy);font-size:21px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.02em"><span style="flex-shrink:0;order:2;color:var(--gold);font-size:20px;line-height:1.3">+</span>How do I know if I need a hearing aid?</summary>
<p style="margin:14px 0 12px;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">A hearing aid may be recommended when a confirmed hearing loss is affecting your daily life. Common signs include difficulty understanding conversations in quiet or in noisy environments, frequently asking others to repeat themselves, or turning the TV up louder than others prefer.</p>
<p style="margin:0;line-height:1.8;text-wrap:pretty">Hearing loss can also take an emotional toll. If conversations with family and friends become frustrating — for you or the people you're talking with — or if you find yourself avoiding social situations because communicating feels stressful or embarrassing, it may be time to explore hearing aids. Persistent ringing in the ears (tinnitus), especially when accompanied by hearing loss, is another reason to schedule a comprehensive hearing evaluation to determine the most appropriate treatment options.</p>
</details>
</div>
